 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A door for «أبواب كل شيء» (leaving before they are seized), geometric for «والحمد لله». No destruction or people drawn. Al-Muyassar's first-person «فتحنا… أعطيناهم… أخذناهم» not used. STAGING v4: 44-45: a nation (three men in dark robes) in a market street; they turn on 44:2 (they left the commands, turning from them); a coins plate on 44:8 for the doors of every worldly thing (both tafsirs: provision, worldly pleasures); they talk on 44:13 (rejoicing in what they were given) and leave on 44:15, well before 44:16; darkness then falls on the empty market (per the caution no destruction is drawn, no one hurt); geometric from 45:7 to the end for the praise. 46 (a hypothetical addressed to the idolaters) stays ambient; mood dawn -> night_sky."
 },
